# mbedtls-mbedtls subpackage
PackageName: mbed_tls
PackageSummary: <text>An open source, portable, easy to use, readable and flexible SSL library with additional features and patches from Espressif.</text>
SPDXID: SPDXRef-SUBPACKAGE-mbedtls-mbedtls
PackageVersion: 3.6.7
PackageSupplier: Organization: Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD
PackageOriginator: Organization: Trusted Firmware <mbed-tls-security@lists.trustedfirmware.org>
PackageDownloadLocation: NOASSERTION
FilesAnalyzed: false
PackageLicenseConcluded: NOASSERTION
PackageLicenseDeclared: NOASSERTION
PackageCopyrightText: NOASSERTION
ExternalRef: SECURITY cpe23Type cpe:2.3:a:arm:mbed_tls:3.6.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*
ExternalRef: SECURITY cpe23Type cpe:2.3:a:trustedfirmware:mbed_tls:3.6.7:*:*:*:*:*:*:*
PackageComment: <text>
# The cve-exclude-list list contains CVEs, which were already evaluated and the package is not vulnerable.
cve-exclude-list:
-   cve: CVE-2026-25832
    reason: TLS 1.3 client accepts a HelloRetryRequest that selects a group it did
        not advertise. The flawed check was added in 3.5.0. Fixed in 3.6.7 by 55ccd932658b
        and in 4.1.1 by cec2cef6b5ce, the 4.1.x fix commit named in the advisory.
        The 4.1.1 ChangeLog lists CVE-2026-25832. The advisory and the CVE record
        name 4.1.2 as the first fixed 4.x release, but the fix is already in the mbedtls-4.1.1
        tag.
-   cve: CVE-2026-73064
    reason: Mbed TLS TLS 1.3 server flaw in 3.2.0 through 3.6.6 and 4.0.0 through
        4.1.0. Fixed in 3.6.7 and 4.1.1
-   cve: CVE-2025-54764
    reason: Fixed in 3.6.5
-   cve: CVE-2025-59438
    reason: Fixed in 3.6.5
-   cve: CVE-2025-52496
    reason: Fixed in 3.6.4
-   cve: CVE-2025-27810
    reason: Fixed in 3.6.3
-   cve: CVE-2025-66442
    reason: Applicable only with Clang with select-optimize feature. ESP-IDF uses
        gcc as the default compiler and uses -Os as the default optimisation flag
# The cve-keywords list includes strings used to search through CVE descriptions.
cve-keywords:
- mbed tls
- mbedtls
</text>

